  "title": "Hypatia of Alexandria",
  "summary": "Hypatia, born in Alexandria about 370 according to MacTutor, was the daughter of the mathematician Theon and taught mathematics and Neoplatonist philosophy. She helped with her father's commentary on Ptolemy's Almagest. A mob, described as mostly Christian monks, killed her in March 415 in a clash tied to the rivalry between Cyril and Orestes.",
